llvmpipe: per-thread decoded-block cache for BPTC (BC7/BC6H) texel fetch

gallivm has no vector BPTC decoder, so every BC7/BC6H texel fell back to a C
fetch that decodes the whole 16-byte block header and endpoints for one texel.
Keep a small per-thread cache of fully decoded 4x4 blocks keyed by block
address, invalidated per scene, compute task and draw. LP_BPTC=0 disables it
for A/B runs (bit 1 cache, bit 2 fetch routing; default 3).
